      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ambient temperature and flour protein content are definitely influencing your levain's stability. Warmer temperatures and higher protein in your flour will generally lead to faster yeast activity and more pronounced pH swings. Try keeping your levain in a consistent, slightly cooler spot and perhaps using a mix with a more stable protein profile to smooth out those sharp shifts. Consistent feeding ratios will also help buffer the microbial activity.",
