      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The transition point where microbial balance breaks down is less a fixed threshold and more a function of environmental stress, nutrient availability, or imbalance. Too much acetic acid buildup, for instance, when the lactic acid bacteria get overwhelmed by anaerobic conditions or rapid yeast fermentation, can cause erratic souring. To stabilize it, focus on keeping your feeding schedule precise and ensuring adequate aeration during peak activity to favor a balanced microbial ecosystem.",
      "source": "target",
